From ae8581711844ac0b65cc0e196b839cc1a228c4df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harvester57 <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] round rational casts to double and float to
 nearest-even

Gmp.Q.add_cast (plugins/e-acsl/src/code_generator/gmp.ml) implemented
ACSL casts (double)r and (float)r on GMP rationals by calling
__gmpq_get_d (and casting the double result to float for (float)r).
GMP's mpq_get_d truncates toward zero, violating ACSL 2.2.5 (which
specifies IEEE 754 round-to-nearest-even):

- true assertions such as `double d = 0.1; assert d == (double)0.1;`
  failed at run time;
- false assertions such as `assert (double)0.1 < 0.1;` and
  `assert 0x1.9999999999999p-4 == (double)0.1;` passed silently;
- (float) casts suffered from both truncation and double rounding
  (e.g. `assert 16777218.0f == (float)16777217.0000000001;` failed).

Add exact IEEE 754 round-to-nearest-even runtime conversion helpers
__e_acsl_mpq_get_d and __e_acsl_mpq_get_f in e_acsl_gmp_api.h and
e_acsl_floating_point.c (handling ties-to-even, subnormals, signs,
underflow, and overflow to +-INFINITY directly on mpz_t operands without
double rounding), call them from Gmp.Q.add_cast, and remove the now
obsolete "R to float: double rounding" warning.

New test: plugins/e-acsl/tests/arith/rational_cast.c; updated existing
E-ACSL oracles referencing __gmpq_get_d.
